25
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:44,040
The Dead Capital Problem (Or: Why Bombs Are the Worst Investment Since Tulips).

26
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:50,890
Here's something nobody tells you: when countries "invest" in military hardware, they're not buying assets.

27
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:55,080
They're buying very expensive paperweights that occasionally explode.

28
00:02:55,900 --> 00:03:01,140
A bridge. It generates economic activity daily (trucks move, people commute, value flows).

29
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:05,380
It lasts fifty to one hundred years. It makes everyone richer.

30
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:10,160
It is pretty to look at. A missile. It sits in a hole doing nothing.

31
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:15,060
It costs one point five million dollars a year just to keep it from rotting.

32
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:19,760
It can only destroy things (including itself). It makes everyone nervous.

33
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:26,460
This is what economists call "dead capital," resources trapped in a form that can't generate returns.

34
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:30,140
It's like if you converted your house into a pile of T.N.T.

35
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:37,500
Sure, it's impressive. But you can't live in it, rent it out, or do anything except eventually blow it up, at which point

36
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:45,260
you have neither a house nor T.N.T. As President Eisenhower (a five-star General who knew about killing professionally)

37
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:54,640
put it: *"Every gun that is made, every warship launched, every rocket fired signifies, in the final sense, a theft from

38
00:03:54,640 --> 00:04:02,920
those who hunger and are not fed, those who are cold and are not clothed."* He literally ran the biggest military in history,

39
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:10,080
and even HE thought you were being ridiculous about this. A one percent treaty doesn't ask you to spend twenty-seven point

40
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:18,279
two billion dollars curing diseases. It asks you to redirect twenty-seven point two billion dollars from the least useful

41
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:23,200
one percent of your military budget to things that make you richer and less dead.

42
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:28,980
It's not spending. It's stopping wasting. The Blueprint for a Saner World.

43
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:35,160
Treaties are magic pieces of paper that countries sign when they want to pretend they'll behave.

44
